    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5e34e19_06a64f18",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/src/board_power.c",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T03:28:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At this point (and with correct `RSMRST` edge configuration) we should deassert `DSW_PWROK`, assert `PWR_EC_PCH_RSMRST`, and wait for both `RSMRST` and `SLP_SUS` to be asserted. So code should be:\n```\n\tpower_signal_set(PWR_EC_SOC_DSW_PWROK, 0);\n\tpower_signal_set(PWR_EC_PCH_RSMRST, 1);\n\n\twhile ((power_signal_get(PWR_RSMRST) \u003d\u003d 0 ||\n\t\tpower_signal_get(PWR_SLP_SUS) \u003d\u003d 0) \u0026\u0026\n\t       timeout_ms \u003e 0) {\n\t\tk_msleep(1);\n\t\ttimeout_ms--;\n\t}\n```\nPlease note that `PWR_EC_PCH_RSMRST` and `RSMRST` edges will be fixed by CL\u0027s in topic: [rsmrst_edge_fix](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/q/topic:%22rsmrst_edge_fix%22). This topic will extend to board specific handlers in non AP_PWRSEQ_DRIVER  version.",
